One thing that wasn't obvious to me: That means taking off all your armor
*and* unwielding your weapon. The "A" command takes some of the drudgery
out of this (you weren't visiting the nurse where other monsters could
intrude, were you?).

And since other parts of this thread mentioned 'trice corpses, a bit of
advice: Always... no, never... forget to put your armor (incl. gloves)
back on after nurse or foocubus encounters. One of my recent characters
would have died but for his "oLS, owing to (1) succubus (2) magic trap =
blind (3) kill 'trice (4) walk on corpse, feel around... fatal mistake.

> 5. Prayer (only if you are under 5 HP, AND can safely pray [every 300
> turns])

The prayer spoiler actually has this listed under "major problems":

  "HP less than or equal to 1/7 maximum (rounded down) or less than 6"

So more than 5 HP can qualify if you're a higher-level character. However,
I learned that *waiting* for your HP to become a "major problem" and
then praying is an unwise strategy... that last hit may very well take
you to 0 HP.

Once actually I was killed in mid-prayer (the monster didn't "start to
attack me but pull back"); I don't recall the circumstances.

